  "details": "Several bindings get disabled when One Handed Movement is enabled while others remain enabled. \n\nFor example, when left radial menu is open, right A button is disabled. So you can no longer jump. Or if right radial menu is open, left A button is disabled so you can no longer mute. But triggers remain functional and keep bindings in and outside of radial menu. \n\nThis has a side effect if using One Handed Movement. If one relies on stick click for Gesture Toggle then it cannot be used when opposite hand radial menu is open. I understand that this just needs to be binded in One Handed mode in SteamVR but it's an example because using Touchpad Down works fine whether radial menu is open or not. Why are some bindings seemingly universal or not.",
